```javascript
function swapAdjectives(sentence) {
  const words = sentence.split(" ");
  let i = 0;
  while (i < words.length - 1) {
    for (let j = i + 1; j < words.length; j++) {
      if (words[i] === "adjective" && words[j] !== "adjective") {
        [words[i], words[j]] = [words[j], words[i]];
      }
    }
    i++;
  }
  return words.join(" ");
}

const originalSentence = "Beautiful green trees are in the park";
const modifiedSentence = swapAdjectives(originalSentence);
console.log(modifiedSentence); // Output: "Green beautiful trees are in the park"
```

This code splits the input sentence into individual words using the `split()` method, then iterates through the array using two nested loops. The outer loop iterates through the array from the first word to the second-last word, while the inner loop iterates through the remaining words from the second word to the last word. If the current word is an adjective and the next word is not an adjective, they are swapped. Finally, the modified sentence is joined back into a string using the `join()` method and returned.

