Here's an Apps Script that searches for a place name in a column and stores the latitude and longitude in other columns:

```javascript
function searchPlace() {
  var sheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSheet();
  var dataRange = sheet.getRange("A2:A"); // Assuming your data starts in cell A2
  var placeName = "New York"; // Replace with the place name you want to search for

  var results = [];

  for (var i = 1; i <= dataRange.getNumRows(); i++) {
    var cell = dataRange.getCell(i, 1);
    if (cell.getValue() === placeName) {
      var latitude = sheet.getRange("B" + i).getValue();
      var longitude = sheet.getRange("C" + i).getValue();

      results.push({
        placeName: cell.getValue(),
        latitude: latitude,
        longitude: longitude
      });
    }
  }

  console.log(results);
}
```

Replace `"New York"` with the place name you want to search for. This script will search for the place name in column A and store the latitude and longitude from columns B and C respectively in the `results` array. You can then use this array to perform further operations or display the results in your spreadsheet.

Here's the PHP custom function "smart_sort_array" as requested:

```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order) {
    usort($set, function ($a, $b) use ($order) {
        return $order === 'asc' ? $a['age'] - $b['age'] : $b['age'] - $a['age'];
    });
    return $set;
}
```

