To set up Auth0 SSO (Single Sign-On) for multiple React apps, follow these steps:

1. Sign up for an Auth0 account and create a new application.
2. In the Auth0 dashboard, navigate to the "Applications" tab and click on your newly created application.
3. Click on the "Settings" tab and scroll down to the "SSO" section.
4. Enable SSO and choose the "SAML 2.0" protocol.
5. Click on the "Create SAML Metadata" button to download the SAML metadata file.
6. Install the `@auth0/auth0-react` package in each of your React apps using npm or yarn.
7. In each app, create a new file called `auth0-config.js` and add the following code:
```javascript
import auth0 from '@auth0/auth0-react';

const auth0Config = {
  domain: 'your-domain.com',
  clientId: 'your-client-id',
  redirectUri: 'http://localhost:3000/callback',
  responseType: 'code id_token token',
  scope: 'openid profile api://your-api-scope',
};

export default auth0Config;
```
Replace `your-domain.com`, `your-client-id`, and `your-api-scope` with the appropriate values from your Auth0 application settings.
8. In each app, import the `auth0-config.js` file and use it to configure the Auth0 provider:
```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { Auth0Provider } from '@auth0/auth0-react';
import auth0Config from './auth0-config';

function App() {
  return (
    <Auth0Provider {...auth0Config}>
      {/* Your app content goes here */}
    </Auth0Provider>
  );
}

export default App;
```
